# Extending equality links
#
# Bob is the same as Robert, and Robert the same as Rob (owl:sameAs). N3
# rules make sameAs symmetric and transitive, so Eyeron links all three
# names to each other and to themselves. A third rule is an inference fuse
# (=> false) for things stated to be both the same and different.

@prefix : <http://example.org/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix list: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/list#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

# Two identity statements
:bob owl:sameAs :robert .
:robert owl:sameAs :rob .

# Rules for owl:sameAs
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

# Symmetry.
{
    ?X owl:sameAs ?Y
} => {
    ?Y owl:sameAs ?X
} .

# Transitivity; with symmetry it also makes each name the same as itself.
{
    ?X owl:sameAs ?Y .
    ?Y owl:sameAs ?Z
} => {
    ?X owl:sameAs ?Z
} .

# Fuse: the same and different at once is a contradiction.
{
    ?X owl:sameAs ?Y .
    ?X owl:differentFrom ?Y
} => false .
